 "notModeled": [
  "analog inputs (differential I+/I-, Q+/Q-), references (REFT/REFB, BG, CML) and PWDN_REF (internal reference power-down, stored nowhere): the result is always the 0 V differential code, mid-scale 80h; the datasheet gives no output-code table (8-bit binary, input range REFB to REFT), so codeFormat offset is the mid-scale reading of a 0 V differential input",
  "SELB output-mode strap: only dual bus mode (SELB low: I data on DA7-DA0, Q data on DB7-DB0, Figure 2) is modeled; single bus mode (SELB high: I and Q alternate on DA7-DA0 at the clock rate, Figure 1) is not",
  "one I/Q sample pair per two CLK cycles (conversion rate fCLK / 2): the model drives the (constant) codes on every CLK rising edge; COUT/COUTBAR are modeled as CLK divided by 2 (and inverted), but their phase to CLK depends on power-on conditions (Figures 1-2, note A)",
  "pipeline latency 5.5 (I) / 6.5 (Q) CLK cycles (the code is constant)",
  "OE enable/disable times (ten/tdis 5 ns) are not modeled separately from tOut",
  "STBY standby: modeled as powerdown (no conversions); the output state during standby is not specified",
